From 0732a858da62316596b533e2eb85aaa53f442daa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pogo-bash <pogo-bash@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 13:02:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb: WebGL image sources upload through a WebGL executor's
 own upload

An executor whose GL is WebGL itself (an embedder without a GPU process) uploads TexImageSource pixels (img, canvas,
video, ImageData, ImageBitmap) with the host's own TexImageSource texImage2D/texSubImage2D/texImage3D/texSubImage3D:
the source's pixels go to it as unpremultiplied RGBA8, and the host converts them to every format and type WebGL
takes, flips and premultiplies as the unpack state says and applies the WebGL 2 unpack sub-rectangle. The Skia export
lost colour under zero alpha, turned LUMINANCE into luma, had no LUMINANCE_ALPHA, 5_5_5_1 or WebGL 2 formats (5_5_5_1
stopped the engine). UNPACK_PREMULTIPLY_ALPHA_WEBGL is ignored for an ImageBitmap, as the spec says.
texImage2D with null pixels sizes its zeroed data by the unpack alignment (an RGB 2x2 upload was INVALID_OPERATION).
Deleting a buffer unbinds it everywhere; bindBufferBase/Range also bind the generic binding point; any buffer may be
bound to the copy targets.
createImageBitmap honours imageOrientation (flipY, and Chrome's "none") and premultiplyAlpha (none keeps the colours
unpremultiplied; default and premultiply premultiply), and takes a video's current frame.
